{"name":"Black Lacquer","hex":"#3f3e3e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"lacquer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A glossy, resinous material used as a surface coating; either a natural exudation of certain trees, or a solution of nitrocellulose in alcohol, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply a lacquer to something or to give something a smooth, glossy finish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lacquer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lacquer","blocks":[{"text":"Lacquer is a type of hard and usually shiny coating or finish applied to materials such as wood or metal. It is most often made from tree sap and wax and has been in use since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/%E6%98%8E%E5%98%89%E9%9D%96_%E5%89%94%E7%B4%85%E5%A3%BD%E5%AD%97%E7%B4%8B%E5%85%AB%E8%A7%92%E6%BC%86%E7%9B%A4-Dish_with_character_for_longevity_%28shou%29_MET_DP704215.jpg/330px-%E6%98%8E%E5%98%89%E9%9D%96_%E5%89%94%E7%B4%85%E5%A3%BD%E5%AD%97%E7%B4%8B%E5%85%AB%E8%A7%92%E6%BC%86%E7%9B%A4-Dish_with_character_for_longevity_%28shou%29_MET_DP704215.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lacquer","wikidata":"Q11236878"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Gourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg/500px-Gourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Gourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg/1280px-Gourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Gourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg/500px-Gourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maki-e sake bottle with Tokugawa clan's mon (emblem), Japan, Edo period","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGourd-Shaped_Sake_Bottle_with_Aoi_Crests.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Plate_made_of_varnished_and_closely-fitted_bamboo%2C_Kinh_ethnic_group%2C_Nam_Dinh_province_-_Vietnam_National_Museum_of_Fine_Arts_-_Hanoi%2C_Vietnam_-_DSC05262.JPG/500px-Plate_made_of_varnished_and_closely-fitted_bamboo%2C_Kinh_ethnic_group%2C_Nam_Dinh_province_-_Vietnam_National_Museum_of_Fine_Arts_-_Hanoi%2C_Vietnam_-_DSC05262.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Plate_made_of_varnished_and_closely-fitted_bamboo%2C_Kinh_ethnic_group%2C_Nam_Dinh_province_-_V